---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Documentation
description: Guides for installing, learning and using Pooka.
permalink: /docs/
---
<section class="page-head">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Documentation</span>
      <h1>Everything, <em>by lantern light</em>.</h1>
      <p>New here? <a href="/docs/install/">Install Pooka</a>, then follow <a href="/docs/getting-started/">Getting started</a>. When you're ready for the whole language, take <a href="/tour/">the tour</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <img class="mascot" src="/assets/mascots/mascot-exploring.png" alt="" width="200">
  </div>
</section>
<section class="section-tight">
  <div class="wrap">
    {%- for group in collections.guides | docsMenu(docs) %}
    <section class="shelf">
      <div class="shelf-head"><h2>{{ group.name }}</h2></div>
      <div class="cards">
        {%- for entry in group.entries %}
        <a class="card" href="{{ entry.url }}"><h3>{{ entry.title }}</h3><p>{{ entry.summary | inlineCode | safe }}</p></a>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
    </section>
    {%- endfor %}
    <div class="notice">
      <img src="/assets/mascots/mascot-curious.png" alt="">
      <div>
        <h3>Looking for an API?</h3>
        <p>The standard library's modules and functions are documented on <a href="{{ site.stdlibDocs }}">HexDocs</a>. Every package's API is generated with <code>pooka docs</code>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
